# Solved is a designation, not a copiable value, kept until the permanent leaves the battlefield (CR 719.3b; the rulings:
# "A solved Case that somehow becomes a copy of a different Case stays solved"). On turn 1 Lion's Eye Diamond discards Bot1's
# hand (delirium: artifact, creature, enchantment, instant), and Shifting Woodland becomes a copy of Case of the Crimson Pulse
# in the graveyard until end of turn. With no cards in hand at the end step its "To solve" makes it solved; the copy ends in
# the cleanup step and the land is still solved. On turn 3 it becomes a copy of Case of the Uneaten Feast, a Case it never
# solved, and is solved at once: Uneaten Feast's "Solved" ability is offered (CR 702.169d), and its sacrifice lets the
# Ornithopter in the graveyard be cast. Neither Case's ability did anything while the Woodland was a land: turn 3's upkeep
# asked for no discard (the hand is the one card drawn).

